            "parts": [
              "I continued 02 and proved a new bound for the complete correction transform:\n\\[\nP_t(x)>\\frac{1}{3000(1+x^2)}\n\\qquad(0\\le t\\le1,\\ x\\in\\mathbb R).\n\\]\nI also derived exact Volterra recovery and a stable source-norm estimate. Computational checks replayed successfully.\n\n**The route now stops at a specific cancellation inequality.** Writing \\(H=A+P\\), \\(\\alpha=A/P\\), and \\(b=P_x/P\\), we need\n\\[\n|1+\\alpha|^2+|\\alpha_x+b(1+\\alpha)|^2\n\\ge\\varepsilon_{\\mathcal R}>0\n\\]\non a declared rectangle, justified using full imaginary Jacobi gluing.\n\nCorrection positivity alone cannot establish this: nearby positive control sources retain the same correction bound while having physical joint zeros.\n\nI prepared a [self-contained ChatGPT brainstorm brief](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/02_angular_jacobi_gluing/reviews/CONTINUATION_AND_BRAINSTORM_BRIEF_20261013.md) with the definitions, new results, failed approaches, and precise question."
